Subtle manual
*************

subtle plays an audio or video file in mpv and shows each subtitle file
(‘.srt’ or ‘.vtt’, up to two at once) as read-only text in Emacs.  The
cue being spoken is highlighted and the text follows the audio.  It is
made for studying a language: the text stays still until the page needs
turning, scrolling by hand pauses the autoscroll, and paragraph layouts
turn cue fragments into running text.

   If you are new, start with the tutorial (‘M-x subtle-tutorial’).
This manual is the full description.  Everything here that mentions a
key shows the key you have bound when read with ‘M-x subtle-manual’, and
the default key in the Info version.

