3.4 Point tracking
==================

Point tracking makes point follow the playback: at every new cue it
jumps to the word a package chose (bltzread: the first unknown one), or
to the start of the cue when none was chosen.  \m switches it on and
off.  Moving point off the cue pauses it (the state is "released") until
point is back on the cue, or the cue reaches the line point is on; then
it tracks again without moving point.  A tracking you switched off stays
off.  Moving point less than ‘subtle-point-track-nav-grace’ seconds
before a cue change releases it as well, so a word you are just reading
is not snatched away.  A card that is open when point moves is
dismissed, and ‘subtle-point-track-moved-functions’ then lets a package
show something for the new word: bltzread opens its card there, so no
key is needed.

Option                           Default   Meaning
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘subtle-point-track-initially’   t         Point jumps to the chosen word of each new cue.
‘subtle-point-track-nav-grace’   0.25      Moving point this many seconds before a cue change releases tracking.
‘subtle-point-track-indicator’   t         Show a small corner box while point tracking is on.


File: subtle.info,  Node: Popups,  Prev: Point tracking,  Up: Options

