8.3.1 Scrolling by hand
-----------------------

Scroll the way you always do.  Autoscroll pauses and a notice appears.
It resumes by itself after a few seconds, or at once when you press ‘r’.
Nothing ever moves the text under you unless the spoken cue has left the
screen.


File: subtle.info,  Node: Trying options live,  Next: A first configuration,  Prev: The keys,  Up: Tutorial

8.4 Trying options live
=======================

Open a session, then press ‘s o’.  It asks for an option and a value,
and the open session changes at once.  Try ‘subtle-text-scale’ with 1.6,
or ‘subtle-layout’ with ‘paragraph-flow’.  Use ‘s v’ as a shortcut for
the layout.

   What you set this way lasts for the Emacs session.  To keep it, put
it in your configuration.


File: subtle.info,  Node: A first configuration,  Next: Hooks (1),  Prev: Trying options live,  Up: Tutorial

8.5 A first configuration
=========================

Options are ordinary Emacs variables.  They live in the ‘subtle’
customization group, so ‘M-x customize-group RET subtle’ works too.  A
handful worth knowing:

     (setopt subtle-text-scale 1.5        ; bigger text (1.0 is your normal size)
             subtle-layout 'paragraph-flow ; running text instead of one cue per line
             subtle-resume-delay 10       ; wait 10 seconds before autoscroll resumes
             subtle-seek-small 10         ; the skip keys jump 10 seconds
             subtle-speed-step 0.1        ; finer speed steps
             subtle-move-point 'never)    ; the cursor stays on the word you study

   Use ‘setopt’ (Emacs 29) so a change in a running session takes effect
at once.  With plain ‘setq’ the new value is used from the next session.

* Menu:

* Layouts: Layouts (1).
* Your own keys::


File: subtle.info,  Node: Layouts (1),  Next: Your own keys,  Up: A first configuration

8.5.1 Layouts
-------------

‘subtle-layout’ decides how cues are arranged:

   • ‘single-spaced’ (the default) is one cue per line.
   • ‘double-spaced’ puts a blank line between cues.
   • ‘sentence’ breaks the line after each sentence.
   • ‘paragraph-flow’ is running text, broken at paragraph breaks.
   • ‘paragraph-pause’ is the same, and playback pauses at each break so
     you can catch up.


File: subtle.info,  Node: Your own keys,  Prev: Layouts (1),  Up: A first configuration

8.5.2 Your own keys
-------------------

The keymap is ‘subtle-mode-map’.  Bind what you like; the strip at the
top and the help box show your keys automatically.

     (with-eval-after-load 'subtle
       (keymap-set subtle-mode-map "SPC" #'subtle-toggle-pause))


